#: src/macros/design.md:6
msgid "Macros In Rust"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:8
msgid ""
"Rust macros provide structured code generation. There are **three kinds** of "
"macros, and **two ways** they are implemented."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:11
msgid "Kinds of Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:13
msgid ""
"**Derive Macros:** Added to type definitions (structs, enums, unions) to "
"auto-implement traits (e.g., `#[derive(Default)]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:15
msgid ""
"**Function-Like Macros:** Invoked with an exclamation mark in item/statement/"
"expr context (e.g., `println!(\"Hello!\")`, `vec![1, 2, 3]`, or "
"`include_bytes!(\"manifest.bin\")`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:18
msgid ""
"**Attribute Macros:** Attached as custom attributes to any item, like "
"functions or modules (e.g., `#[tokio::main]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:21
msgid "Implementation Forms"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:23
msgid ""
"**Declarative Macros (AKA \"Macros By Example\"):** Part of the language "
"itself, based on pattern matching; these can only be used to define function-"
"like macros."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:26
msgid ""
"**Procedural Macros:** Rust functions running as compiler plugins that "
"transform token streams. These can perform arbitrary operations at compile "
"time, including I/O if desired."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:33
msgid ""
"Highlight that students have already used function-like macros (like "
"`println!`, `vec!`, `format!`) and derive macros (like `#[derive(Clone, "
"Debug)]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/design.md:36
msgid ""
"Explain that attribute macros are very popular in libraries like Tokio or "
"Axum, often transforming functions similar to Python decorators."
msgstr ""
